      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey, i need some help writing a performance review for one of my senior account executives. they've been doing great with client retention and keeping our big accounts happy, but they keep showing up late to our internal morning stand-up meetings. i want to be constructive but firm about the punctuality thing. can you help me draft something?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I can help you draft a performance review that's both constructive and firm. You might want to start by acknowledging their strengths, like their excellent client retention skills, and then gently address the issue of tardiness. Here's a possible draft:\n\n\"[Senior Account Executive's Name], I wanted to take a moment to discuss your performance over the past quarter. Your exceptional work with client retention has been a significant asset to our team, and I'm grateful for your dedication to keeping our big accounts happy. However, I've noticed that you've been consistently late to our internal morning stand-up meetings, which can impact our team's ability to move forward with projects and discuss important updates.\n\nI understand that occasional tardiness can be unavoidable, but the frequency of your late arrivals has become a concern. I'd like to encourage you to make a greater effort to arrive on time, as this will not only show respect for your colleagues but also demonstrate your commitment to our team's success.\n\nTo support you in this area, I'd like to propose a few strategies. Firstly, I can work with you to identify any potential roadblocks that may be causing your tardiness, such as transportation issues or unexpected delays. Secondly, I can offer to adjust the meeting schedule to",
